{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- context.json ---'\ncat /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/outputs/space_overview/subspace--metaphysics/context.json\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- records files ---'\nfind /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/sources/records -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- claims files ---'\nfind /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/claims -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- relations files ---'\nfind /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/relations -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- topics files ---'\nfind /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/topics -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort\"","aggregated_output":"--- context.json ---\n{\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:08:29Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-a-fact-p-is-fully-grounded-in-d-only-if-the-connecting-question-asking-why-p-obt--ea3a1a698124\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"significance: [p] is fully grounded in D only if the connecting questions with respect to [p] and D lack cognitive significance.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Grounding Requires Insignificance\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\",\n      \"text\": \"A fact [p] is fully grounded in D only if the connecting question asking why [p] obtains given D lacks cognitive significance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-a-subsumption-theoretic-version-of-grounding-says-that-p1-p2-and-so-on-ground-q--fe650fc0cecd\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Say that p is quasi-subsumed by q (in symbols: p \\u2272 q) iff there is some r such that p \\u2227 r \\u2264 q. Replacing \\u2291\\u2228 with \\u2264 in our original account of grounding, and \\u2291\\u2227\\u2228 with \\u2272, delivers the following subsumption-theoretic analogue: (18) p1, p2, \\u2026 < q iff: (i) p1 \\u00d9 p 2 \\u00d9 \\u2026 \\u2264 q; and (ii) neither q \\u2272 p1, nor q \\u2272 p2, nor \\u2026\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Subsumption refines grounding\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"A subsumption-theoretic version of grounding says that p1, p2, and so on ground q exactly when their conjunction is subsumed by q while q is not quasi-subsumed by any of them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-a-species-of-grounding-in-which-a-truthmaker-grounds-t--9c9dc5afedc6\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Whenever an entity is a truthmaker of a proposition, that entity is the alethic-fact ground of the fact that the proposition is true.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Truthmakers ground truth-facts\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Alethic-fact grounding is a species of grounding in which a truthmaker grounds the fact that the truthmade proposition is true.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-non-irreflexive-because-if-proposition-b-is-true-and-s--0f3a01a46967\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"If proposition B is true, the fact that B is true is grounded in the fact stated by B; where B says that B is true, the fact grounds itself.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Alethic grounding is reflexive\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Alethic-fact grounding is non-irreflexive because if proposition B is true and says that B is true, the fact that B is true grounds itself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:08:29Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-apparent-counterexamples-to-grounding-necessity-fail-when-alleged-full-grounds-a--8cbbd720ef13\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Dancy-style, universal-fact, and widowhood cases need extra explanatorily relevant facts; the rose-mode case mistakes a non-ground for a ground.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Counterexamples Misidentify Grounds\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Apparent counterexamples to grounding necessity fail when alleged full grounds are reclassified as partial grounds requiring additional explanatorily relevant facts or as non-grounds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-ceremonial-psychedelic-use-increased-fatalistic-determinism-at-four-weeks-in-the--f71a027b70cc\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The psychedelic ceremony was associated with increases in scores of Fatalistic determinism at 4 weeks versus baseline (t(121) = 2.81, p = 0.012, d = 0.25, 95% CI [0.06, 0.37]); however, this effect did not persist at 6 months.\",\n        \"For psychedelic-na\\u00efve participants ... the changes persisted for at least 6 months (t(52) = 2.86, p = 0.012, d = 0.39, 95% CI [0.11, 0.64]).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Fatalism rises temporarily\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Ceremonial psychedelic use increased fatalistic determinism at four weeks in the overall prospective sample, but this effect did not persist to six months except in the psychedelic-naive subgroup.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:08:29Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-connecting-questions-lack-cognitive-significance-only-when-fine-style-essential--f96bc70d5d2d\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"essence: lack of cognitive significance requires essential truths characteristic of the relevant facts or entities according to which \\u2227D \\u2192 p.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Essence Explains Insignificance\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Connecting questions lack cognitive significance only when Fine-style essential truths about [p], D, their plurality, or involved entities make \\u2227D imply p.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:42:50Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-episodic-recollection-can-preserve-temporally-and-spatially-situated-autobiograp--43867278649d\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Almost immediately following his accident, R.B. was able to intentionally recall specific events temporally and spatially situated in his personal past, but his recollection of those events was compromised in an unusual manner \\u2014 memory for those events, though fitting the standard criteria for episodic recollection, was not accompanied by a sense of personal ownership.\",\n        \"I was remembering scenes, not facts \\u2026 I could clearly recall a scene of me at the beach in New London with my family as a child. But the feeling was that the scene was not my memory. As if I was looking at a photo of someone else\\u2019s vacation.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Episodic memory lacks ownership\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\",\n      \"text\": \"Episodic recollection can preserve temporally and spatially situated autobiographical content while lacking a felt sense of personal ownership.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-factual-grounding-is-analyzed-through-disjunctive-parthood-a-plurality-of-facts--d0a2dc4b2f48\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"FACTUAL-GROUNDING p1, p2, \\u2026 < q iff: (i) p1 \\u00d9 p2 \\u00d9 \\u2026 \\u2291\\u2228 q; and (ii) neither q \\u2291\\u2227\\u2228 p1, nor q \\u2291\\u2227\\u2228 p2, nor \\u2026\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Grounding uses disjunctive parthood\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"Factual grounding is analyzed through disjunctive parthood: a plurality of facts grounds q exactly when their conjunction is a disjunctive part of q and q is not a relevant conjunctive-disjunctive part of any ground.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-full-generic-essence-is-captured-by-generalized-identity-being-f-is-what-it-is-t--96f5798ed301\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"FULL-GENERIC-ESSENCE Being F is what it is to be G in full iff: for a thing to be G is for it to be F (in symbols: Gx \\u00bax Fx).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Full essence is identity\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"Full generic essence is captured by generalized identity: being F is what it is to be G in full exactly when, for a thing to be G, is for it to be F.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-generalized-identity-is-a-non-factive-no-difference-operator-that-can-apply-to-f--7cb985988184\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"we express generalized identity with an operator, \\u00ba, indexed by zero or more variables, which takes two open or closed sentences and yields another. Where p and q are open or closed sentences, (5) p\\u00baq should be read as 'For it to be the case that p is for it to be the case that q'.\",\n        \"we read such statements as not requiring that the flanking expressions be true/satisfied: for instance, it is intuitively no objection to (1) that there aren\\u2019t any bachelors. For short, we read them non-factively.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Generalized identity is nonfactive\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"Generalized identity is a non-factive no-difference operator that can apply to factual and generic contents without requiring fact-shaped or property-shaped entities as its relata.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-greater-lifetime-psychedelic-use-correlates-with-stronger-baseline-panpsychist-b--a024d2968b54\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"A significant positive correlation was found between previous psychedelic use and shifts away from the hard-materialism pole of the hard-materialism vs. hard-dualism spectrum at baseline (r = 0.223, p < 0.0001).\",\n        \"Lifetime psychedelic use was positively correlated with panpsychist views and negatively correlated with hard materialistic views measured at baseline.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Past use predicts panpsychism\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Greater lifetime psychedelic use correlates with stronger baseline panpsychist beliefs and weaker baseline hard materialist beliefs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-ground-theoretic-status-is-preserved-under-factual-identity-because-the-proposed--4aecebbdb4a2\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"given that generalized identity is symmetric and transitive, and that the rules R3 and R4 are truth-preserving, FACTUAL-GROUNDING entails that ground-theoretic status is preserved under factual identity. More precisely: (17) a. If p, p1, p2 \\u2026 ground q and p \\u00ba p* , then p*, p1, p2, \\u2026 ground q. b. If p1, p2, \\u2026 ground q and q \\u00ba q*, then p1, p2, \\u2026 ground q*.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Identity preserves grounding status\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"Ground-theoretic status is preserved under factual identity because the proposed account combines generalized identity with symmetric and transitive identity principles.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-grounding-and-essence-can-both-be-analyzed-in-terms-of-generalized-identity-yiel--e2abdab353f9\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"We develop a unified and uniform account of grounding and essence, one which understands them both in terms of a generalized notion of identity examined in recent work by Fabrice Correia, Cian Dorr, Agust\\u00edn Rayo, and others.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Generalized identity unifies metaphysics\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"Grounding and essence can both be analyzed in terms of generalized identity, yielding a unified and uniform account of how the two metaphysical notions interact.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-grounding-does-not-entail-being-more-fundamental-than-so-appeals-to-relative-fun--0468a01c8a45\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Bottomless or dense grounding chains are used to argue that x can ground y without x being closer to a fundamental entity than y.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Grounding need not imply fundamentality\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Grounding does not entail being more fundamental than, so appeals to relative fundamentality do not rule out reflexive or symmetric grounding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order-because-it-is-neither-transitive-irreflexive-nor--0dc6a102d51b\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"A strict order is a relation that is transitive, irreflexive, and asymmetric; the source argues that grounding lacks all three features.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Grounding lacks strict order\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Grounding is not a strict order because it is neither transitive, irreflexive, nor asymmetric.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:08:29Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-grounding-necessity-is-not-secured-merely-by-treating-grounding-as-a-determinati--23325d0a6e99\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Causation is a determination relation but is not plausibly iii-style necessary; necessary truths can also have merely partial grounds.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Modal Definitions Fail\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Grounding necessity is not secured merely by treating grounding as a determination relation or by defining full grounding in modal terms.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:08:29Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-if-a-fact-p-is-fully-grounded-in-a-plurality-of-facts-d-then-the-conjunction-of--dbb969101dbd\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"necessity: if [p] is fully grounded in D, then \\u25a1(\\u2227D \\u2192 p).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Full Grounds Entail Truth\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\",\n      \"text\": \"If a fact [p] is fully grounded in a plurality of facts D, then the conjunction of the propositions corresponding to D metaphysically necessitates p.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-if-being-f-grounds-being-g-then-the-fact-that-being-f-necessitates-being-g-can-b--685ae4dcbfb4\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"if being F grounds being G, our account implies that being G just is being F or H for some given H, and which on our account gives the (or a) full essence of being G. It then follows that necessarily, a thing is G iff it is F or H, which entails by straightforward modal reasoning that necessarily, a thing is F only if it\\u2019s also G, as desired.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Grounding yields necessitation\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"If being F grounds being G, then the fact that being F necessitates being G can be derived from what it is to be G.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-in-a-randomized-controlled-depression-trial-psilocybin-therapy-produced-shifts-a--7cfb0c0f75e7\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"A significant drug versus time interaction was observed (F(56) = 3.13, p = 0.041, one-tailed).\",\n        \"Post-hoc tests reveal that shifts away from hard materialism were evident in the psilocybin group only (Z = 2.28, p = 0.02, d = 0.45). The escitalopram group showed no changes in NPB (Z = 0.24, p = 0.33, d = 0.2).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Psilocybin shifts materialism\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"In a randomized controlled depression trial, psilocybin therapy produced shifts away from hard materialism at six weeks whereas escitalopram did not.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-most-psychedelic-associated-shifts-in-non-physicalist-metaphysical-beliefs-persi--9591d5bd7c0c\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"These changes were sustained 6 months after the ceremony (t(121) = 5.07, p < 0.0001, d = 0.46, 95% CI [0.22, 0.50]).\",\n        \"The observed changes were enduring, persisting for up to 6 months in most domains, with the exception of fatalistic determinism.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Belief shifts partly endure\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Most psychedelic-associated shifts in non-physicalist metaphysical beliefs persisted for at least six months, while fatalistic determinism was less durable in the overall observational sample.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-necessary-entailment-or-equivalence-is-not-sufficient-for-essence-because-genera--162946956228\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"being Socrates and such that there are infinitely many prime numbers is necessarily entailed by and equivalent to being Socrates, yet presumably the former is ground-theoretically linked to the arithmetic realm in ways that the latter isn\\u2019t. Given our account, this provides reason to believe that the former isn\\u2019t part of the essence of the latter either, as desired.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Necessity underdetermines essence\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"Necessary entailment or equivalence is not sufficient for essence, because generalized identity and grounding can distinguish essential structure from merely necessary coextension.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-objectual-essence-can-be-accounted-for-through-generic-essence-so-a-feature-is-w--bd5daa95f779\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Following Correia (2006, pp. 764-5) we account for objectual essence in terms of generic essence: FULL-OBJECTUAL-ESSENCE Being F is what x is in full iff: being F is what it is to be identical to x in full.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Objectual essence tracks identity\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"Objectual essence can be accounted for through generic essence, so a feature is what an object is in full or in part according to whether it is what being identical to that object is in full or in part.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:08:29Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-paradigm-grounding-cases-support-the-significance-principle-because-their-connec--28555377f52b\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"For [p\\u2228q] grounded in [p], the question why [p\\u2228q] obtains given [p] lacks cognitive significance.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Paradigms Support Significance\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Paradigm grounding cases support the significance principle because their connecting questions lack substantive content even for individuals with little detailed knowledge of the relevant facts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:22:07Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-partial-generic-essence-is-captured-by-conjunctive-partial-generalized-identity--13ec1cd27c1f\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"PARTIAL-GENERIC-ESSENCE Being F is partially what it is to be G iff: there is some H such that for a thing to be G is for it to be both F and H (in symbols: Gx \\u00bax Fx \\u00d9 Hx).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Partial essence is conjunctive\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\",\n      \"text\": \"Partial generic essence is captured by conjunctive partial generalized identity: being F is partially what it is to be G exactly when being G is being both F and some H.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-participants-with-no-prior-psychedelic-experience-showed-larger-shifts-away-from--056a417d978d\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Their first psychedelic experience ... significant changes found at 4 weeks (t(52) = 3.85, p = 0.001, d = 0.53, 95% CI [0.21, 0.66]) and 6 months (t(52) = 5.32, p < 0.0001, d = 0.73, 95% CI [0.36, 0.80]).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Naive users shift more\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Participants with no prior psychedelic experience showed larger shifts away from physicalism than the full observational sample.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-patients-who-clinically-responded-to-psilocybin-therapy-showed-greater-shifts-aw--b78b1f525f61\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Significantly greater shifts away from hard materialistic beliefs were found for those patients who showed a clinically meaningful response to psilocybin only ... versus those who showed a response to escitalopram (Z = 1.74, p = 0.041, g = 0.56, 90% CI [\\u2212 0.17, 1.26]).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Psilocybin response shifts beliefs\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Patients who clinically responded to psilocybin therapy showed greater shifts away from hard materialist beliefs than patients who responded to escitalopram.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-perceived-emotional-synchrony-during-the-psychedelic-ceremony-mediates-later-cha--adcb9ca374b4\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Results supported a model with excellent fit in which perceived \\u2018emotional synchrony\\u2019 with other participants\\u2014moderated by baseline scores of peer conformity\\u2014predicted subsequent changes in the NPB factor.\",\n        \"Figure 4. Changes in non-physicalist beliefs are moderated by baseline variables and pre-state identify fusion and mediated by acute emotional synchrony during the psychedelic session.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Synchrony mediates belief change\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Perceived emotional synchrony during the psychedelic ceremony mediates later changes in non-physicalist beliefs, with baseline peer conformity moderating that pathway.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-psychedelic-use-is-associated-with-significant-shifts-away-from-hard-physicalist--b7e61a4e9b3c\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Pooling scores for the NPB factor, analyses revealed a significant shift away from physicalism at 4 weeks compared with baseline (t(121) = 3.66, p = 0.001, d = 0.33, 95% CI [0.12, 0.39]).\",\n        \"The Non-Physicalist Beliefs factor included positive loadings for beliefs in supernatural realms, non-natural unifying principles, panpsychism, dualism, and solipsism/idealism, while materialism and naturalism loaded negatively.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Psychedelics reduce hard materialism\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Psychedelic use is associated with significant shifts away from hard physicalist or materialist metaphysical beliefs and toward non-physicalist positions such as panpsychism, dualism, and non-naturalism.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:42:50Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-quasi-memory-accounts-must-specify-which-form-of-self-representation-is-required--4b048f888bc8\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The notion of quasi-memory is supposed to undergird a theory of personal identity, but which (if any) of these self-representations is required in order for a candidate quasi-memory to count as being \\u2018caused in the normal way\\u2019?\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Quasi-memory needs self criteria\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\",\n      \"text\": \"Quasi-memory accounts must specify which form of self-representation is required for causally normal memory to constitute personal identity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:42:50Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-r-b-retained-factual-self-knowledge-trait-self-knowledge-voluntary-scene-recall--fc36edde2153\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"I can recall memories [from the non-ownership period of his life] at will. I have normal control over remembering facts and scenes from my past. But when I remember scenes from before the injury, they do not feel as if they happened to me \\u2014 though intellectually I know that they did \\u2014 they felt as if they happened to someone else.\",\n        \"During the un-owned period I was able to plan for the future. Although my working memory loss and lack of skill at compensation made it challenging.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"R.B. retained future planning\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\",\n      \"text\": \"R.B. retained factual self-knowledge, trait self-knowledge, voluntary scene recall, and some future planning despite lacking ownership for many pre-injury memories.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:42:50Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-r-b-s-unowned-recollections-provide-an-existence-proof-for-apparent-memory-conte--6a14bce7e1a3\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"R.B.\\u2019s recollections provide an existence proof for a kind of memory that navigates between the horns of Schechtman\\u2019s dilemma. In R.B., the \\u2018mineness\\u2019 of episodic recollection is separated from the content.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"R.B. answers quasi-memory\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\",\n      \"text\": \"R.B.'s unowned recollections provide an existence proof for apparent memory content that is neither delusional nor identity-presupposing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-schaffer-s-contrastive-or-differential-formulation-of-grounding-still-fails-to-m--7fd859e88bdc\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The fact that B is true rather than not true grounds itself, and E-is-true-rather-than-not-true and F-is-true-rather-than-not-true ground each other.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Differential grounding remains non-strict\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Schaffer's contrastive or differential formulation of grounding still fails to make grounding a strict order because the same examples violate differential irreflexivity and differential asymmetry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-schaffer-s-set-based-counterexample-does-not-establish-grounding-non-transitivit--49174a1f51f7\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The source says Schaffer's support for the set case treats counterfactual necessity as sufficient in one step and necessary in another, while determinable-determinate and disjunctive cases undermine that test.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Schaffer counterexample is inconclusive\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Schaffer's set-based counterexample does not establish grounding non-transitivity because it relies on an unstable counterfactual-necessity test.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-shifts-away-from-hard-materialism-are-positively-associated-with-increases-in-ps--4bb5f88069f2\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"A significant positive correlation was found between shifts away from hard-materialism (the NPB factor) and changes in well-being. The correlation was significant at 4 weeks and at 6 months post-ceremony.\",\n        \"Figure 3. Shifts away from hard materialistic beliefs are associated with increases in well-being.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Belief change tracks wellbeing\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"Shifts away from hard materialism are positively associated with increases in psychological well-being after psychedelic ceremonies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:32:25Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-combined-prospective-correlational-mechanistic-and-controlled-trial-evidence--bb114d52608c\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"These lines of evidence include: (1) that the belief-shifts were observed prospectively ... (5) independent data from a separate controlled study in a different population, replicated our observational research findings.\",\n        \"The study did not collect respondents\\u2019 and patients\\u2019 religious affiliations at baseline, differential environmental susceptibilities, or interests concerning metaphysical beliefs.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Causality remains context-limited\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\",\n      \"text\": \"The combined prospective, correlational, mechanistic, and controlled-trial evidence supports a possible causal influence of psychedelic use on metaphysical belief change, while remaining limited by sample selection and contextual confounds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:08:29Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-conjunction-of-the-significance-principle-the-essence-principle-and-the-meta--4f212a9f1869\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Formal chain: grounding plus significance gives cognitive insignificance; essence gives \\u2227D \\u2192 p; essential truths are metaphysically necessary; therefore \\u25a1(\\u2227D \\u2192 p).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Essence Yields Necessity\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\",\n      \"text\": \"The conjunction of the significance principle, the essence principle, and the metaphysical necessity of essential truths yields the necessity of grounding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:08:29Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-epistemic-constraint-on-grounding-does-not-undermine-grounding-objectivity-b--87922d9890f9\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The constraint ties grounding to general epistemic facts about which questions have substantive content for suitably situated individuals.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Epistemic Constraint Is Objective\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\",\n      \"text\": \"The epistemic constraint on grounding does not undermine grounding objectivity because it concerns general epistemic facts rather than any particular subject\\u2019s ignorance or capacities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:42:50Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-evidential-force-of-memory-for-personal-identity-depends-on-the-contingent-c--ef23d993b2fe\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Knowing the nature of the systems that deliver these judgements might be an important source of information for evaluating the extent to which the sense of identity can be taken to reflect the reality of identity.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Memory evidence is contingent\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\",\n      \"text\": \"The evidential force of memory for personal identity depends on the contingent cognitive systems that generate ownership feelings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:42:50Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-memory-based-sense-of-personal-identity-depends-on-at-least-two-separable-co--f9eaee4ce165\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The apparent paradox \\u2014 episodic memory of past events absent the feeling of personal ownership \\u2014 can be understood by situating episodic memory in the context of a system of interrelated memory processes, some of which provide the raw data for experience and some of which enable the experience to be \\u2018mine\\u2019.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Identity sense has components\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\",\n      \"text\": \"The memory-based sense of personal identity depends on at least two separable components: event content and a mechanism that supplies mineness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:42:50Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-sense-of-numerical-personal-identity-is-a-contingent-feature-of-episodic-mem--b672a3618f23\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"As we have seen, the sense of personal identity given by episodic memory is robust \\u2014 it gives us an \\u2018irresistible\\u2019 sense of being the same person, and it has seemed to many to be a necessary concomitant of episodic memory. But the case of R.B. indicates that this sense of identity is dissociable from episodic memory itself. The sense of identity turns out to be, pace Reid, a contingent feature of memory.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Mineness is contingent\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\",\n      \"text\": \"The sense of numerical personal identity is a contingent feature of episodic memory rather than a necessary output of episodic recall.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:42:50Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-trait-self-knowledge-can-remain-accurate-and-resilient-even-when-episodic-memory--e1d296edc23e\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"There now exists an extensive database showing that even patients suffering total anterograde and retrograde episodic amnesia can describe their own personal characteristics both reliably and accurately.\",\n        \"D.B. had knowledge of his own traits, and yet he was \\u2018unaware that he had a past and unable to imagine what his experiences might be like in the future\\u2019.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Trait self is insufficient\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\",\n      \"text\": \"Trait self-knowledge can remain accurate and resilient even when episodic memory no longer supports a sense of diachronic personal identity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-truthmaking-and-alethic-fact-grounding-are-non-asymmetric-because-distinct-propo--9d116dfbb4b5\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"For C = <D exists> and D = <C exists>, D truthmakes C and C truthmakes D; for E = <F is true> and F = <E is true>, their truth-facts ground each other.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Mutual grounding defeats asymmetry\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Truthmaking and alethic-fact grounding are non-asymmetric because distinct propositions can mutually truthmake or ground each other's truth facts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-truthmaking-is-a-species-of-grounding-because-the-relation-between-a-truthmaker--4d84e79d3baf\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The relation between truthmaker and truth is compared with member-set, part-whole, and cruel-action/wrong-action relations as initially plausible grounding cases.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Truthmaking is grounding\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Truthmaking is a species of grounding because the relation between a truthmaker and what is true is analogous to standard ground-grounded relations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-truthmaking-is-non-irreflexive-because-a-proposition-of-the-form-e-exists-is-mad--d4aca38737b4\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Truthmaker theory is said to be committed to propositions of the form <e exists> being made true by e; if proposition A exists, it is made true by itself.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Truthmaking permits self-truthmakers\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Truthmaking is non-irreflexive because a proposition of the form <e exists> is made true by e, so an existing proposition can make true its own existence claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T15:15:18Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-truthmaking-is-non-transitive-socrates-being-white-truthmakes-the-proposition-th--3fbb8a3c9b9d\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"(1) The fact that Socrates is white makes <Socrates is white> true. (2) <Socrates is white> makes <There are propositions> true. Transitivity would yield (3), but the source rejects (3).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Truthmaking is nontransitive\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\",\n      \"text\": \"Truthmaking is non-transitive: Socrates' being white truthmakes the proposition that Socrates is white, and that proposition truthmakes that there are propositions, but Socrates' being white does not truthmake that there are propositions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"freshness\": {\n    \"claim_count\": 46,\n    \"generated_at\": \"2026-04-26T18:11:17Z\",\n    \"input_signature\": \"sha256:af34e79548489cc84615d74295dbddb6b6fe91ddf0f26d16a3ca377e0069ea66\",\n    \"relation_count\": 29,\n    \"source_record_count\": 5,\n    \"topic_count\": 12\n  },\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"overview_id\": \"su