{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\nCTX=/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/outputs/space_overview/subspace--metaphysics/context.json\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- source records ---'\njq -r '.source_records[] | [.source_id, .title, (.authors // [] | join(\\\"; \\\")), (.year // \\\"\\\"), (.summary // .abstract // .description // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' \\\"\"'$CTX\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- claims compact ---'\njq -r '.claims[] | [.claim_id, .source_id, .short_title, .text] | @tsv' \\\"\"'$CTX\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- relations compact ---'\njq -r '.relations[]? | [.relation_id, .relation_type, (.source_claim_id // .from_claim_id // .subject_claim_id // \\\"\\\"), (.target_claim_id // .to_claim_id // .object_claim_id // \\\"\\\"), (.description // .text // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' \\\"\"'$CTX\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- topics compact ---'\njq -r '.topics[]? | [.topic_id, .title, (.summary // .description // \\\"\\\"), ((.claim_ids // []) | join(\\\",\\\")), ((.source_ids // []) | join(\\\",\\\"))] | @tsv' \\\"\"'$CTX\"'","aggregated_output":"--- source records ---\nsource-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\t01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent\tKelly Trogdon\t\tKelly Trogdon argues that full grounding is necessary: whenever [p] is fully grounded in D, the propositions corresponding to D metaphysically entail p. The argument relies on an epistemic significance constraint and a Fine-style essence principle, then answers apparent counterexamples by distinguishing full grounds from partial grounds and non-grounds.\nsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\t02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order\tGonzalo Rodriguez-Pereyra\t\tGonzalo Rodriguez-Pereyra argues that grounding is not a strict order. The paper builds the case through truthmaking and alethic-fact grounding, rejects Schaffer's set-based transitivity counterexample as inconclusive, then offers formal examples against transitivity, irreflexivity, and asymmetry.\nsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\t03-grounding-essence-and-identity\tFabrice Correia; Alexander Skiles\t\tCorreia and Skiles argue that generalized identity can provide a unified analysis of grounding and essence. Full and partial essence are modeled through generic identity and conjunctive parthood, while grounding is modeled through disjunctive parthood and subsumption. The resulting framework aims to explain why grounding implies certain essence-based necessitation patterns without collapsing essence into mere modal equivalence.\nsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\t04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs\tChristopher Timmermann; Hannes Kettner; Chris Letheby; Leor Roseman; Fernando E. Rosas; Robin L. Carhart-Harris\t\tTimmermann and colleagues report that psychedelic use is associated with shifts away from hard materialist metaphysical beliefs toward non-physicalist views, with convergent evidence from a prospective ceremony survey and a smaller controlled psilocybin therapy trial. The strongest results concern non-physicalist belief change, persistence to six months, mediation by emotional synchrony, and association with improved well-being or depression response, while publication date metadata could not be resolved from the local record.\nsource-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\t05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity\tStanley B. Klein; Shaun Nichols\t\tKlein and Nichols use the neurological case of patient R.B. to argue that episodic memory content can be dissociated from the sense of personal ownership or mineness. The paper proposes a component model of memory-based personal identity and applies it to debates over quasi-memory and the evidential value of memory for persistence of self.\n--- claims compact ---\nclaim-a-fact-p-is-fully-grounded-in-d-only-if-the-connecting-question-asking-why-p-obt--ea3a1a698124\tsource-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\tGrounding Requires Insignificance\tA fact [p] is fully grounded in D only if the connecting question asking why [p] obtains given D lacks cognitive significance.\nclaim-a-subsumption-theoretic-version-of-grounding-says-that-p1-p2-and-so-on-ground-q--fe650fc0cecd\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tSubsumption refines grounding\tA subsumption-theoretic version of grounding says that p1, p2, and so on ground q exactly when their conjunction is subsumed by q while q is not quasi-subsumed by any of them.\nclaim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-a-species-of-grounding-in-which-a-truthmaker-grounds-t--9c9dc5afedc6\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tTruthmakers ground truth-facts\tAlethic-fact grounding is a species of grounding in which a truthmaker grounds the fact that the truthmade proposition is true.\nclaim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-non-irreflexive-because-if-proposition-b-is-true-and-s--0f3a01a46967\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tAlethic grounding is reflexive\tAlethic-fact grounding is non-irreflexive because if proposition B is true and says that B is true, the fact that B is true grounds itself.\nclaim-apparent-counterexamples-to-grounding-necessity-fail-when-alleged-full-grounds-a--8cbbd720ef13\tsource-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\tCounterexamples Misidentify Grounds\tApparent counterexamples to grounding necessity fail when alleged full grounds are reclassified as partial grounds requiring additional explanatorily relevant facts or as non-grounds.\nclaim-ceremonial-psychedelic-use-increased-fatalistic-determinism-at-four-weeks-in-the--f71a027b70cc\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tFatalism rises temporarily\tCeremonial psychedelic use increased fatalistic determinism at four weeks in the overall prospective sample, but this effect did not persist to six months except in the psychedelic-naive subgroup.\nclaim-connecting-questions-lack-cognitive-significance-only-when-fine-style-essential--f96bc70d5d2d\tsource-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\tEssence Explains Insignificance\tConnecting questions lack cognitive significance only when Fine-style essential truths about [p], D, their plurality, or involved entities make ∧D imply p.\nclaim-episodic-recollection-can-preserve-temporally-and-spatially-situated-autobiograp--43867278649d\tsource-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\tEpisodic memory lacks ownership\tEpisodic recollection can preserve temporally and spatially situated autobiographical content while lacking a felt sense of personal ownership.\nclaim-factual-grounding-is-analyzed-through-disjunctive-parthood-a-plurality-of-facts--d0a2dc4b2f48\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tGrounding uses disjunctive parthood\tFactual grounding is analyzed through disjunctive parthood: a plurality of facts grounds q exactly when their conjunction is a disjunctive part of q and q is not a relevant conjunctive-disjunctive part of any ground.\nclaim-full-generic-essence-is-captured-by-generalized-identity-being-f-is-what-it-is-t--96f5798ed301\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tFull essence is identity\tFull generic essence is captured by generalized identity: being F is what it is to be G in full exactly when, for a thing to be G, is for it to be F.\nclaim-generalized-identity-is-a-non-factive-no-difference-operator-that-can-apply-to-f--7cb985988184\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tGeneralized identity is nonfactive\tGeneralized identity is a non-factive no-difference operator that can apply to factual and generic contents without requiring fact-shaped or property-shaped entities as its relata.\nclaim-greater-lifetime-psychedelic-use-correlates-with-stronger-baseline-panpsychist-b--a024d2968b54\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tPast use predicts panpsychism\tGreater lifetime psychedelic use correlates with stronger baseline panpsychist beliefs and weaker baseline hard materialist beliefs.\nclaim-ground-theoretic-status-is-preserved-under-factual-identity-because-the-proposed--4aecebbdb4a2\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tIdentity preserves grounding status\tGround-theoretic status is preserved under factual identity because the proposed account combines generalized identity with symmetric and transitive identity principles.\nclaim-grounding-and-essence-can-both-be-analyzed-in-terms-of-generalized-identity-yiel--e2abdab353f9\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tGeneralized identity unifies metaphysics\tGrounding and essence can both be analyzed in terms of generalized identity, yielding a unified and uniform account of how the two metaphysical notions interact.\nclaim-grounding-does-not-entail-being-more-fundamental-than-so-appeals-to-relative-fun--0468a01c8a45\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tGrounding need not imply fundamentality\tGrounding does not entail being more fundamental than, so appeals to relative fundamentality do not rule out reflexive or symmetric grounding.\nclaim-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order-because-it-is-neither-transitive-irreflexive-nor--0dc6a102d51b\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tGrounding lacks strict order\tGrounding is not a strict order because it is neither transitive, irreflexive, nor asymmetric.\nclaim-grounding-necessity-is-not-secured-merely-by-treating-grounding-as-a-determinati--23325d0a6e99\tsource-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\tModal Definitions Fail\tGrounding necessity is not secured merely by treating grounding as a determination relation or by defining full grounding in modal terms.\nclaim-if-a-fact-p-is-fully-grounded-in-a-plurality-of-facts-d-then-the-conjunction-of--dbb969101dbd\tsource-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\tFull Grounds Entail Truth\tIf a fact [p] is fully grounded in a plurality of facts D, then the conjunction of the propositions corresponding to D metaphysically necessitates p.\nclaim-if-being-f-grounds-being-g-then-the-fact-that-being-f-necessitates-being-g-can-b--685ae4dcbfb4\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tGrounding yields necessitation\tIf being F grounds being G, then the fact that being F necessitates being G can be derived from what it is to be G.\nclaim-in-a-randomized-controlled-depression-trial-psilocybin-therapy-produced-shifts-a--7cfb0c0f75e7\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tPsilocybin shifts materialism\tIn a randomized controlled depression trial, psilocybin therapy produced shifts away from hard materialism at six weeks whereas escitalopram did not.\nclaim-most-psychedelic-associated-shifts-in-non-physicalist-metaphysical-beliefs-persi--9591d5bd7c0c\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tBelief shifts partly endure\tMost psychedelic-associated shifts in non-physicalist metaphysical beliefs persisted for at least six months, while fatalistic determinism was less durable in the overall observational sample.\nclaim-necessary-entailment-or-equivalence-is-not-sufficient-for-essence-because-genera--162946956228\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tNecessity underdetermines essence\tNecessary entailment or equivalence is not sufficient for essence, because generalized identity and grounding can distinguish essential structure from merely necessary coextension.\nclaim-objectual-essence-can-be-accounted-for-through-generic-essence-so-a-feature-is-w--bd5daa95f779\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tObjectual essence tracks identity\tObjectual essence can be accounted for through generic essence, so a feature is what an object is in full or in part according to whether it is what being identical to that object is in full or in part.\nclaim-paradigm-grounding-cases-support-the-significance-principle-because-their-connec--28555377f52b\tsource-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\tParadigms Support Significance\tParadigm grounding cases support the significance principle because their connecting questions lack substantive content even for individuals with little detailed knowledge of the relevant facts.\nclaim-partial-generic-essence-is-captured-by-conjunctive-partial-generalized-identity--13ec1cd27c1f\tsource-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\tPartial essence is conjunctive\tPartial generic essence is captured by conjunctive partial generalized identity: being F is partially what it is to be G exactly when being G is being both F and some H.\nclaim-participants-with-no-prior-psychedelic-experience-showed-larger-shifts-away-from--056a417d978d\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tNaive users shift more\tParticipants with no prior psychedelic experience showed larger shifts away from physicalism than the full observational sample.\nclaim-patients-who-clinically-responded-to-psilocybin-therapy-showed-greater-shifts-aw--b78b1f525f61\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tPsilocybin response shifts beliefs\tPatients who clinically responded to psilocybin therapy showed greater shifts away from hard materialist beliefs than patients who responded to escitalopram.\nclaim-perceived-emotional-synchrony-during-the-psychedelic-ceremony-mediates-later-cha--adcb9ca374b4\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tSynchrony mediates belief change\tPerceived emotional synchrony during the psychedelic ceremony mediates later changes in non-physicalist beliefs, with baseline peer conformity moderating that pathway.\nclaim-psychedelic-use-is-associated-with-significant-shifts-away-from-hard-physicalist--b7e61a4e9b3c\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tPsychedelics reduce hard materialism\tPsychedelic use is associated with significant shifts away from hard physicalist or materialist metaphysical beliefs and toward non-physicalist positions such as panpsychism, dualism, and non-naturalism.\nclaim-quasi-memory-accounts-must-specify-which-form-of-self-representation-is-required--4b048f888bc8\tsource-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\tQuasi-memory needs self criteria\tQuasi-memory accounts must specify which form of self-representation is required for causally normal memory to constitute personal identity.\nclaim-r-b-retained-factual-self-knowledge-trait-self-knowledge-voluntary-scene-recall--fc36edde2153\tsource-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\tR.B. retained future planning\tR.B. retained factual self-knowledge, trait self-knowledge, voluntary scene recall, and some future planning despite lacking ownership for many pre-injury memories.\nclaim-r-b-s-unowned-recollections-provide-an-existence-proof-for-apparent-memory-conte--6a14bce7e1a3\tsource-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\tR.B. answers quasi-memory\tR.B.'s unowned recollections provide an existence proof for apparent memory content that is neither delusional nor identity-presupposing.\nclaim-schaffer-s-contrastive-or-differential-formulation-of-grounding-still-fails-to-m--7fd859e88bdc\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tDifferential grounding remains non-strict\tSchaffer's contrastive or differential formulation of grounding still fails to make grounding a strict order because the same examples violate differential irreflexivity and differential asymmetry.\nclaim-schaffer-s-set-based-counterexample-does-not-establish-grounding-non-transitivit--49174a1f51f7\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tSchaffer counterexample is inconclusive\tSchaffer's set-based counterexample does not establish grounding non-transitivity because it relies on an unstable counterfactual-necessity test.\nclaim-shifts-away-from-hard-materialism-are-positively-associated-with-increases-in-ps--4bb5f88069f2\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tBelief change tracks wellbeing\tShifts away from hard materialism are positively associated with increases in psychological well-being after psychedelic ceremonies.\nclaim-the-combined-prospective-correlational-mechanistic-and-controlled-trial-evidence--bb114d52608c\tsource-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\tCausality remains context-limited\tThe combined prospective, correlational, mechanistic, and controlled-trial evidence supports a possible causal influence of psychedelic use on metaphysical belief change, while remaining limited by sample selection and contextual confounds.\nclaim-the-conjunction-of-the-significance-principle-the-essence-principle-and-the-meta--4f212a9f1869\tsource-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\tEssence Yields Necessity\tThe conjunction of the significance principle, the essence principle, and the metaphysical necessity of essential truths yields the necessity of grounding.\nclaim-the-epistemic-constraint-on-grounding-does-not-undermine-grounding-objectivity-b--87922d9890f9\tsource-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\tEpistemic Constraint Is Objective\tThe epistemic constraint on grounding does not undermine grounding objectivity because it concerns general epistemic facts rather than any particular subject’s ignorance or capacities.\nclaim-the-evidential-force-of-memory-for-personal-identity-depends-on-the-contingent-c--ef23d993b2fe\tsource-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\tMemory evidence is contingent\tThe evidential force of memory for personal identity depends on the contingent cognitive systems that generate ownership feelings.\nclaim-the-memory-based-sense-of-personal-identity-depends-on-at-least-two-separable-co--f9eaee4ce165\tsource-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\tIdentity sense has components\tThe memory-based sense of personal identity depends on at least two separable components: event content and a mechanism that supplies mineness.\nclaim-the-sense-of-numerical-personal-identity-is-a-contingent-feature-of-episodic-mem--b672a3618f23\tsource-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\tMineness is contingent\tThe sense of numerical personal identity is a contingent feature of episodic memory rather than a necessary output of episodic recall.\nclaim-trait-self-knowledge-can-remain-accurate-and-resilient-even-when-episodic-memory--e1d296edc23e\tsource-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4\tTrait self is insufficient\tTrait self-knowledge can remain accurate and resilient even when episodic memory no longer supports a sense of diachronic personal identity.\nclaim-truthmaking-and-alethic-fact-grounding-are-non-asymmetric-because-distinct-propo--9d116dfbb4b5\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tMutual grounding defeats asymmetry\tTruthmaking and alethic-fact grounding are non-asymmetric because distinct propositions can mutually truthmake or ground each other's truth facts.\nclaim-truthmaking-is-a-species-of-grounding-because-the-relation-between-a-truthmaker--4d84e79d3baf\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tTruthmaking is grounding\tTruthmaking is a species of grounding because the relation between a truthmaker and what is true is analogous to standard ground-grounded relations.\nclaim-truthmaking-is-non-irreflexive-because-a-proposition-of-the-form-e-exists-is-mad--d4aca38737b4\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tTruthmaking permits self-truthmakers\tTruthmaking is non-irreflexive because a proposition of the form <e exists> is made true by e, so an existing proposition can make true its own existence claim.\nclaim-truthmaking-is-non-transitive-socrates-being-white-truthmakes-the-proposition-th--3fbb8a3c9b9d\tsource-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\tTruthmaking is nontransitive\tTruthmaking is non-transitive: Socrates' being white truthmakes the proposition that Socrates is white, and that proposition truthmakes that there are propositions, but Socrates' being white does not truthmake that there are propositions.\n--- relations compact ---\nderived_from:claim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-non-irreflexive-because-if-proposition-b-is-true-and-s--0f3a01a46967->claim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-a-species-of-grounding-in-which-a-truthmaker-grounds-t--9c9dc5afedc6\tderived_from\t\t\t\nderived_from:claim-factual-grounding-is-analyzed-through-disjunctive-parthood-a-plurality-of-facts--d0a2dc4b2f48->claim-grounding-and-essence-can-both-be-analyzed-in-terms-of-generalized-identity-yiel--e2abdab353f9\tderived_from\t\t\t\nderived_from:claim-full-generic-essence-is-captured-by-generalized-identity-being-f-is-what-it-is-t--96f5798ed301->claim-grounding-and-essence-can-both-be-analyzed-in-terms-of-generalized-identity-yiel--e2abdab353f9\tderived_from\t\t\t\nderived_from:claim-most-psychedelic-associated-shifts-in-non-physicalist-metaphysical-beliefs-persi--9591d5bd7c0c->claim-psychedelic-use-is-associated-with-significant-shifts-away-from-hard-physicalist--b7e61a4e9b3c\tderived_from\t\t\t\nderived_from:claim-partial-generic-essence-is-captured-by-conjunctive-partial-generalized-identity--13ec1cd27c1f->claim-grounding-and-essence-can-both-be-analyzed-in-terms-of-generalized-identity-yiel--e2abdab353f9\tderived_from\t\t\t\nderived_from:claim-quasi-memory-accounts-must-specify-which-form-of-self-representation-is-required--4b048f888bc8->claim-r-b-s-unowned-recollections-provide-an-existence-proof-for-apparent-memory-conte--6a14bce7e1a3\tderived_from\t\t\t\nsimilar:claim-patients-who-clinically-responded-to-psilocybin-therapy-showed-greater-shifts-aw--b78b1f525f61|claim-shifts-away-from-hard-materialism-are-positively-associated-with-increases-in-ps--4bb5f88069f2\ts