{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\nCTX=/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/outputs/space_overview/subspace--metaphysics/context.json\nfor sid in \\\\\n source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0 \\\\\n source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3 \\\\\n source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e \\\\\n source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0 \\\\\n source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4; do\n  printf '%s\\\\n' \\\"--- \"'$sid ---\"\n  jq -r --arg sid \"$sid\" '\"'.claims[] | select(.source_id==\"'$sid) | [.claim_id, .short_title, .text] | @tsv'\"' \\\"\"'$CTX\"\ndone'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\nCTX=/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/outputs/space_overview/subspace--metaphysics/context.json\nfor sid in \\\\\n source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0 \\\\\n source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3 \\\\\n source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e \\\\\n source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0 \\\\\n source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4; do\n  printf '%s\\\\n' \\\"--- \"'$sid ---\"\n  jq -r --arg sid \"$sid\" '\"'.claims[] | select(.source_id==\"'$sid) | [.claim_id, .short_title, .text] | @tsv'\"' \\\"\"'$CTX\"\ndone'","aggregated_output":"--- source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0 ---\nclaim-a-fact-p-is-fully-grounded-in-d-only-if-the-connecting-question-asking-why-p-obt--ea3a1a698124\tGrounding Requires Insignificance\tA fact [p] is fully grounded in D only if the connecting question asking why [p] obtains given D lacks cognitive significance.\nclaim-apparent-counterexamples-to-grounding-necessity-fail-when-alleged-full-grounds-a--8cbbd720ef13\tCounterexamples Misidentify Grounds\tApparent counterexamples to grounding necessity fail when alleged full grounds are reclassified as partial grounds requiring additional explanatorily relevant facts or as non-grounds.\nclaim-connecting-questions-lack-cognitive-significance-only-when-fine-style-essential--f96bc70d5d2d\tEssence Explains Insignificance\tConnecting questions lack cognitive significance only when Fine-style essential truths about [p], D, their plurality, or involved entities make ∧D imply p.\nclaim-grounding-necessity-is-not-secured-merely-by-treating-grounding-as-a-determinati--23325d0a6e99\tModal Definitions Fail\tGrounding necessity is not secured merely by treating grounding as a determination relation or by defining full grounding in modal terms.\nclaim-if-a-fact-p-is-fully-grounded-in-a-plurality-of-facts-d-then-the-conjunction-of--dbb969101dbd\tFull Grounds Entail Truth\tIf a fact [p] is fully grounded in a plurality of facts D, then the conjunction of the propositions corresponding to D metaphysically necessitates p.\nclaim-paradigm-grounding-cases-support-the-significance-principle-because-their-connec--28555377f52b\tParadigms Support Significance\tParadigm grounding cases support the significance principle because their connecting questions lack substantive content even for individuals with little detailed knowledge of the relevant facts.\nclaim-the-conjunction-of-the-significance-principle-the-essence-principle-and-the-meta--4f212a9f1869\tEssence Yields Necessity\tThe conjunction of the significance principle, the essence principle, and the metaphysical necessity of essential truths yields the necessity of grounding.\nclaim-the-epistemic-constraint-on-grounding-does-not-undermine-grounding-objectivity-b--87922d9890f9\tEpistemic Constraint Is Objective\tThe epistemic constraint on grounding does not undermine grounding objectivity because it concerns general epistemic facts rather than any particular subject’s ignorance or capacities.\n--- source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3 ---\nclaim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-a-species-of-grounding-in-which-a-truthmaker-grounds-t--9c9dc5afedc6\tTruthmakers ground truth-facts\tAlethic-fact grounding is a species of grounding in which a truthmaker grounds the fact that the truthmade proposition is true.\nclaim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-non-irreflexive-because-if-proposition-b-is-true-and-s--0f3a01a46967\tAlethic grounding is reflexive\tAlethic-fact grounding is non-irreflexive because if proposition B is true and says that B is true, the fact that B is true grounds itself.\nclaim-grounding-does-not-entail-being-more-fundamental-than-so-appeals-to-relative-fun--0468a01c8a45\tGrounding need not imply fundamentality\tGrounding does not entail being more fundamental than, so appeals to relative fundamentality do not rule out reflexive or symmetric grounding.\nclaim-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order-because-it-is-neither-transitive-irreflexive-nor--0dc6a102d51b\tGrounding lacks strict order\tGrounding is not a strict order because it is neither transitive, irreflexive, nor asymmetric.\nclaim-schaffer-s-contrastive-or-differential-formulation-of-grounding-still-fails-to-m--7fd859e88bdc\tDifferential grounding remains non-strict\tSchaffer's contrastive or differential formulation of grounding still fails to make grounding a strict order because the same examples violate differential irreflexivity and differential asymmetry.\nclaim-schaffer-s-set-based-counterexample-does-not-establish-grounding-non-transitivit--49174a1f51f7\tSchaffer counterexample is inconclusive\tSchaffer's set-based counterexample does not establish grounding non-transitivity because it relies on an unstable counterfactual-necessity test.\nclaim-truthmaking-and-alethic-fact-grounding-are-non-asymmetric-because-distinct-propo--9d116dfbb4b5\tMutual grounding defeats asymmetry\tTruthmaking and alethic-fact grounding are non-asymmetric because distinct propositions can mutually truthmake or ground each other's truth facts.\nclaim-truthmaking-is-a-species-of-grounding-because-the-relation-between-a-truthmaker--4d84e79d3baf\tTruthmaking is grounding\tTruthmaking is a species of grounding because the relation between a truthmaker and what is true is analogous to standard ground-grounded relations.\nclaim-truthmaking-is-non-irreflexive-because-a-proposition-of-the-form-e-exists-is-mad--d4aca38737b4\tTruthmaking permits self-truthmakers\tTruthmaking is non-irreflexive because a proposition of the form <e exists> is made true by e, so an existing proposition can make true its own existence claim.\nclaim-truthmaking-is-non-transitive-socrates-being-white-truthmakes-the-proposition-th--3fbb8a3c9b9d\tTruthmaking is nontransitive\tTruthmaking is non-transitive: Socrates' being white truthmakes the proposition that Socrates is white, and that proposition truthmakes that there are propositions, but Socrates' being white does not truthmake that there are propositions.\n--- source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e ---\nclaim-a-subsumption-theoretic-version-of-grounding-says-that-p1-p2-and-so-on-ground-q--fe650fc0cecd\tSubsumption refines grounding\tA subsumption-theoretic version of grounding says that p1, p2, and so on ground q exactly when their conjunction is subsumed by q while q is not quasi-subsumed by any of them.\nclaim-factual-grounding-is-analyzed-through-disjunctive-parthood-a-plurality-of-facts--d0a2dc4b2f48\tGrounding uses disjunctive parthood\tFactual grounding is analyzed through disjunctive parthood: a plurality of facts grounds q exactly when their conjunction is a disjunctive part of q and q is not a relevant conjunctive-disjunctive part of any ground.\nclaim-full-generic-essence-is-captured-by-generalized-identity-being-f-is-what-it-is-t--96f5798ed301\tFull essence is identity\tFull generic essence is captured by generalized identity: being F is what it is to be G in full exactly when, for a thing to be G, is for it to be F.\nclaim-generalized-identity-is-a-non-factive-no-difference-operator-that-can-apply-to-f--7cb985988184\tGeneralized identity is nonfactive\tGeneralized identity is a non-factive no-difference operator that can apply to factual and generic contents without requiring fact-shaped or property-shaped entities as its relata.\nclaim-ground-theoretic-status-is-preserved-under-factual-identity-because-the-proposed--4aecebbdb4a2\tIdentity preserves grounding status\tGround-theoretic status is preserved under factual identity because the proposed account combines generalized identity with symmetric and transitive identity principles.\nclaim-grounding-and-essence-can-both-be-analyzed-in-terms-of-generalized-identity-yiel--e2abdab353f9\tGeneralized identity unifies metaphysics\tGrounding and essence can both be analyzed in terms of generalized identity, yielding a unified and uniform account of how the two metaphysical notions interact.\nclaim-if-being-f-grounds-being-g-then-the-fact-that-being-f-necessitates-being-g-can-b--685ae4dcbfb4\tGrounding yields necessitation\tIf being F grounds being G, then the fact that being F necessitates being G can be derived from what it is to be G.\nclaim-necessary-entailment-or-equivalence-is-not-sufficient-for-essence-because-genera--162946956228\tNecessity underdetermines essence\tNecessary entailment or equivalence is not sufficient for essence, because generalized identity and grounding can distinguish essential structure from merely necessary coextension.\nclaim-objectual-essence-can-be-accounted-for-through-generic-essence-so-a-feature-is-w--bd5daa95f779\tObjectual essence tracks identity\tObjectual essence can be accounted for through generic essence, so a feature is what an object is in full or in part according to whether it is what being identical to that object is in full or in part.\nclaim-partial-generic-essence-is-captured-by-conjunctive-partial-generalized-identity--13ec1cd27c1f\tPartial essence is conjunctive\tPartial generic essence is captured by conjunctive partial generalized identity: being F is partially what it is to be G exactly when being G is being both F and some H.\n--- source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0 ---\nclaim-ceremonial-psychedelic-use-increased-fatalistic-determinism-at-four-weeks-in-the--f71a027b70cc\tFatalism rises temporarily\tCeremonial psychedelic use increased fatalistic determinism at four weeks in the overall prospective sample, but this effect did not persist to six months except in the psychedelic-naive subgroup.\nclaim-greater-lifetime-psychedelic-use-correlates-with-stronger-baseline-panpsychist-b--a024d2968b54\tPast use predicts panpsychism\tGreater lifetime psychedelic use correlates with stronger baseline panpsychist beliefs and weaker baseline hard materialist beliefs.\nclaim-in-a-randomized-controlled-depression-trial-psilocybin-therapy-produced-shifts-a--7cfb0c0f75e7\tPsilocybin shifts materialism\tIn a randomized controlled depression trial, psilocybin therapy produced shifts away from hard materialism at six weeks whereas escitalopram did not.\nclaim-most-psychedelic-associated-shifts-in-non-physicalist-metaphysical-beliefs-persi--9591d5bd7c0c\tBelief shifts partly endure\tMost psychedelic-associated shifts in non-physicalist metaphysical beliefs persisted for at least six months, while fatalistic determinism was less durable in the overall observational sample.\nclaim-participants-with-no-prior-psychedelic-experience-showed-larger-shifts-away-from--056a417d978d\tNaive users shift more\tParticipants with no prior psychedelic experience showed larger shifts away from physicalism than the full observational sample.\nclaim-patients-who-clinically-responded-to-psilocybin-therapy-showed-greater-shifts-aw--b78b1f525f61\tPsilocybin response shifts beliefs\tPatients who clinically responded to psilocybin therapy showed greater shifts away from hard materialist beliefs than patients who responded to escitalopram.\nclaim-perceived-emotional-synchrony-during-the-psychedelic-ceremony-mediates-later-cha--adcb9ca374b4\tSynchrony mediates belief change\tPerceived emotional synchrony during the psychedelic ceremony mediates later changes in non-physicalist beliefs, with baseline peer conformity moderating that pathway.\nclaim-psychedelic-use-is-associated-with-significant-shifts-away-from-hard-physicalist--b7e61a4e9b3c\tPsychedelics reduce hard materialism\tPsychedelic use is associated with significant shifts away from hard physicalist or materialist metaphysical beliefs and toward non-physicalist positions such as panpsychism, dualism, and non-naturalism.\nclaim-shifts-away-from-hard-materialism-are-positively-associated-with-increases-in-ps--4bb5f88069f2\tBelief change tracks wellbeing\tShifts away from hard materialism are positively associated with increases in psychological well-being after psychedelic ceremonies.\nclaim-the-combined-prospective-correlational-mechanistic-and-controlled-trial-evidence--bb114d52608c\tCausality remains context-limited\tThe combined prospective, correlational, mechanistic, and controlled-trial evidence supports a possible causal influence of psychedelic use on metaphysical belief change, while remaining limited by sample selection and contextual confounds.\n--- source-05-memory-and-the-sense-of-personal-identity--a1fbe0966ca4 ---\nclaim-episodic-recollection-can-preserve-temporally-and-spatially-situated-autobiograp--43867278649d\tEpisodic memory lacks ownership\tEpisodic recollection can preserve temporally and spatially situated autobiographical content while lacking a felt sense of personal ownership.\nclaim-quasi-memory-accounts-must-specify-which-form-of-self-representation-is-required--4b048f888bc8\tQuasi-memory needs self criteria\tQuasi-memory accounts must specify which form of self-representation is required for causally normal memory to constitute personal identity.\nclaim-r-b-retained-factual-self-knowledge-trait-self-knowledge-voluntary-scene-recall--fc36edde2153\tR.B. retained future planning\tR.B. retained factual self-knowledge, trait self-knowledge, voluntary scene recall, and some future planning despite lacking ownership for many pre-injury memories.\nclaim-r-b-s-unowned-recollections-provide-an-existence-proof-for-apparent-memory-conte--6a14bce7e1a3\tR.B. answers quasi-memory\tR.B.'s unowned recollections provide an existence proof for apparent memory content that is neither delusional nor identity-presupposing.\nclaim-the-evidential-force-of-memory-for-personal-identity-depends-on-the-contingent-c--ef23d993b2fe\tMemory evidence is contingent\tThe evidential force of memory for personal identity depends on the contingent cognitive systems that generate ownership feelings.\nclaim-the-memory-based-sense-of-personal-identity-depends-on-at-least-two-separable-co--f9eaee4ce165\tIdentity sense has components\tThe memory-based sense of personal identity depends on at least two separable components: event content and a mechanism that supplies mineness.\nclaim-the-sense-of-numerical-personal-identity-is-a-contingent-feature-of-episodic-mem--b672a3618f23\tMineness is contingent\tThe sense of numerical personal identity is a contingent feature of episodic memory rather than a necessary output of episodic recall.\nclaim-trait-self-knowledge-can-remain-accurate-and-resilient-even-when-episodic-memory--e1d296edc23e\tTrait self is insufficient\tTrait self-knowledge can remain accurate and resilient even when episodic memory no longer supports a sense of diachronic personal identity.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
